  "title": "Blog Department Week v0.6",
  "description": "One week of the blog department, observed from the vault: post front matter (BLOG_DEPARTMENT stages 1-2) and, since v0.2, the drafting cron's per-run reports in ops/blog-runs (v0.2 P1). Counts only: no titles, keywords, URLs or text. runs is null when the report folder is not mounted, never zero. Since v0.3, stages: each BLOG_DEPARTMENT v0.2 stage's progress towards its switch condition (P2 verify, P3 analysis, P4a kw_replay, P4b kw_direct, P5 feedback, P6 instruction, P7 slot), counts and dates only; a stage with no record is null, never zero. Since v0.4, the P4a/P4b keyword stages carry the newest run of agreeing bundle days as a calendar span (run_first, run_last, run_days both ends included, run_bundle_days) in place of days_agreeing_in_a_row: root's cron leaves a bundle only on full-run days, and the switch condition counts fourteen calendar days. A gap of more than three days between bundle days ends the run. Since v0.5, the P6 instruction stage carries the week's affiliate placements against the morning instruction's pick (P7, Thomas 2026-11-05): placed, matched, differed, unjudged, and the instructions that could not read the affiliate stock. Since v0.6, stages.watch: the outsourced-side watch (blog_watch, P6 prerequisite, Thomas 2026-11-05): the KST days it recorded, its latest problems, and per check the week's days with a problem.",
